Package: chwrite
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3
Description: protect files in a Git repository from unwanted modification
 chwrite is a dependency-free command-line tool that lets a Git repository
 declare files or directories that should not be modified by coding agents,
 scripts, editors, or other processes.
 .
 It applies the strongest file-protection mechanism available on the local
 operating system (chflags uchg on macOS, chattr/chmod on Linux, ACLs on
 Windows) and can verify protected files before Git operations such as
 commit or push. The core implementation is a single dependency-free
 Python 3 file; this package installs it plus a small POSIX shell launcher.
